      "status": "pass",
      "unit": "requested answer roles and fields"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The original Phase2 domain is recorded Final Report Resolution information. Its original CQ3 main Spec-contributor question expressly reuses Company, Spec, REFERENCES and submittedBy/modifies. Hence the original-context population is companies attributed through retained Resolution-reference paths to documents modifying the named Spec. Agreement-only, latest release, approved CR, human leadership and world-zero company populations are not imposed. This reads the named main-contributor question in its authored Resolution domain, rather than replacing it with ownership truth.",
      "original_quote": "contributors to spec 38.331",
      "query_clauses": [
        "MATCH (r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec {specNumber:'38.331'})",
        "(t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)"
      ],
      "status": "pass",
      "unit": "population and source context"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Original CQ3 source coverage explicitly says references→Tdoc→submittedBy and Spec association uses modifies; it also specifies the relevant reused classes/relationships. The submitted document company receives recorded contribution attribution when its document is referenced by a Resolution and modifies this Spec. Citation is not approval, adoption, causal success or legal ownership. Unlike a new post-repair exception, this exact relationship contract is present in the actual indexed design independently of original query/results. The query implements it with all Resolution subtypes.",
      "original_quote": "contributors to spec 38.331",
      "query_clauses": [
        "(r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)",
        "(t)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec)",
        "sp.specNumber='38.331'",
        "(t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)"
      ],
      "status": "pass",
      "unit": "filters and relationship meaning"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The original CQ3 source frames company Resolution contribution, with Resolution as the decision-record domain and REFERENCES as the attribution relation. The metric is one distinct recorded Resolution attributed to each company, not each path, each co-submitted TDoc, or each Spec release node. count(DISTINCT r) preserves that contribution unit under multi-document, multi-company or release-specific joins. A co-submitter can be attributed once for the same Resolution without an invented fractional credit rule.",
      "original_quote": "Rank the main contributors",
      "query_clauses": [
        "count(DISTINCT r) AS contributionCount",
        "group by c.companyName"
      ],
      "status": "pass",
      "unit": "counting unit and join multiplicity"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The original indexed CQ3 result rule explicitly defines TopN default10, and unchanged English requests a rank of main contributors without overriding N. This source supplies ten rather than relying solely on old LIMIT10 or choosing a cutoff by fiat. The reference query retains the full uncapped positive-path ranking population; the answer contract takes min(10,population) and preserves boundary groups. The original Count DESC/Company ASC secondary key is part of this documented default. No full real-world contributors claim or arbitrary extra minimum contribution threshold is introduced.",
      "original_quote": "main contributors",
      "query_clauses": [
        "no LIMIT in full reference query",
        "collection.kind=top_k_boundary_ties",
        "cardinality_policy.mode=top_k,value=10"
      ],
      "status": "pass",
      "unit": "cardinality and completeness"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Rank requires order. Original CQ3 Count DESC and Company ASC source rules justify the exact numeric count primary and company-name secondary keys. Requiring this declared order differs from importing an unspecified chronological proxy. Equal complete source-key groups permit any within-group presentation and boundary subset. The full uncapped source pool is necessary to apply the quota; no lexicographic TDoc or latest-meeting shortcut is used.",
      "original_quote": "Rank",
      "query_clauses": [
        "ORDER BY contributionCount DESC, companyName ASC",
        "require_rank_order=true",
        "source_order_keys=contributionCount DESC/companyName ASC"
      ],
      "status": "pass",
      "unit": "ordering and ties when requested"
    },
    {
      "finding": "This exact source-context record ranking answers the main contributor request; RRC ownership remains an unverified practical interpretation of contribution, not a measured legal or causal claim. The unchanged original term is retained and that boundary must be disclosed. Neither original source matrix nor the query establishes technical adoption, normative incorporation, world authorship completeness or expert endorsement; none is made a required answer field. Native/full independent answer SQL/scorer controls remain later gates and are not supplied by this semantic judgment.",
